WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.448
A business receives nine hundred dollars covering two invoices. Sealwork helps match those private

00:00:05.448 --> 00:00:09.728
records and pays the worker only after the agreed checks pass.

00:00:10.278 --> 00:00:17.061
I ask the hiring agent to choose within my rules. It uses public build history, recommends a

00:00:17.061 --> 00:00:21.051
reviewed executable, and cannot change my budget or payment destination.

00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:27.822
I review the fictional invoices and bank records. The bank-analysis path encrypts the private input

00:00:27.822 --> 00:00:31.969
for NEAR AI Cloud, separately from the public hiring decision.

00:00:32.519 --> 00:00:38.919
The live private model proposes allocating nine hundred dollars across five hundred and four hundred

00:00:38.919 --> 00:00:44.039
dollar invoices. The ambiguous two hundred fifty dollar payment stays Needs review.

00:00:44.589 --> 00:00:51.455
I review the proposed matches and acceptance rules before funding. The model’s suggestion is only a

00:00:51.455 --> 00:00:55.747
proposal. A separate deterministic verifier will check the original records.

00:00:56.297 --> 00:01:03.322
The worker fee is zero point zero five testnet NEAR. It pays for processing; it does not move the

00:01:03.322 --> 00:01:06.281
fictional bank payment. I approve the pinned-build agreement.

00:01:06.831 --> 00:01:12.254
The worker and separate verifier execute privately through OutLayer. The checks pass, NEAR escrow

00:01:12.254 --> 00:01:16.516
settles the fee, and the receipt now says Verified and paid.

00:01:17.066 --> 00:01:23.504
I can inspect the checked private report. The combined payment matches, and the ambiguous item

00:01:23.504 --> 00:01:27.797
remains open. The public receipt excludes the plaintext financial records.

00:01:28.347 --> 00:01:34.619
Both execution records identify the agreed binary fingerprints. NEAR holds the budget, processes

00:01:34.619 --> 00:01:40.891
authenticated callbacks and records the outcome. Full hardware evidence is linked for inspection.

00:01:41.441 --> 00:01:47.380
Opening the same receipt in a separate page shows encrypted delivery. Public visitors can inspect

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:51.339
settlement and evidence, but they cannot read the private report.

00:01:51.889 --> 00:01:58.203
Importing the private recovery file restores access to the report. Keep that file private. Its

00:01:58.203 --> 00:02:02.833
access material is excluded from the repository and this demo evidence.

00:02:03.383 --> 00:02:10.286
Finally, this genuine earlier faulty-build receipt is rejected and refunded. Its failure belongs to

00:02:10.286 --> 00:02:16.202
that code version. Sealwork combines confidential work, independent checks and conditional NEAR

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:16.695
payment.
